10
01:11:25,714 --> 01:11:31,714
Tenet is a 2020 science fiction action thriller film written and directed by
Christopher Nolan, who also produced it with his wife Emma Thomas.

11
01:18:34,285 --> 01:18:40,285
It stars John David Washington, Robert Pattinson, Elizabeth Debicki,
Dimple Kapadia, Michael Caine, and Kenneth Branagh.

12
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
The film follows a former CIA officer who is recruited into a secret organization, tasked with tracing the origin of objects
that are traveling backward through time and their connection to an attack from the future to the present.

13
01:32:51,428 --> 01:32:57,428
Nolan took over five years to write the screenplay after deliberating
about Tenet's central ideas for more than a decade.

14
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
Pre-production began in late 2018, casting took place in March 2019, and
principal photography lasted six months in multiple countries.

15
01:47:08,571 --> 01:47:14,571
After delays due to the COVID-19 pandemic, Tenet was released in the United Kingdom
on August 26, 2020, and in the United States on September 3, 2020.

16
01:54:17,142 --> 01:54:23,142
It was Nolan's last film to be released by Warner Bros.

17
02:01:25,714 --> 02:01:31,714
Tenet was the first Hollywood tent-pole to open in theaters during the pandemic and grossed $365 million worldwide on a
$205 million budget, making it the fifth-highest-grossing film of 2020 despite failing to break even.

18
02:08:34,285 --> 02:08:40,285
The film divided critics but won Best Visual Effects at the 93rd
Academy Awards and received numerous other accolades.

19
02:15:42,857 --> 02:15:48,857
The film explores themes of assassin, espionage, spy,
time travel, mumbai (bombay), india.

20
02:22:51,428 --> 02:22:57,428
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
